(>> 1.1 Structural Taxonomy of English Parts of Speech) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Professional scientific communication demands rigorous adherence to grammatical syntax,) Tj
T*
(clarity, and precision.) Tj
T*
(* Nouns and Nominalization: Proper, Common, Collective, Abstract, and Material nouns.) Tj
T*
(- Countable vs. Uncountable Nouns: Countable nouns \(cell, enzyme, molecule\) take) Tj
T*
(plural forms and indefinite articles. Uncountable nouns \(biomass, DNA, water,) Tj
T*
(equipment, information\) take singular verbs and cannot take indefinite articles or) Tj
T*
(plural suffixes \(*equipments is strictly ungrammatical\).) Tj
T*
(* Pronouns: Subjective \(I, he, they\), Objective \(me, him, them\), Possessive \(my, his,) Tj
T*
(their\), Demonstrative \(this, that, these, those\), Relative \(who, which, that, whose\).) Tj
T*
(- Relative Pronoun Distinction: 'Which' introduces non-restrictive \(parenthetical\)) Tj
T*
(clauses preceded by a comma; 'That' introduces restrictive \(essential\) clauses) Tj
T*
(without commas.) Tj
T*
(* Verbs: Finite \(carries tense, number, person\) vs. Non-Finite \(Gerunds [-ing) Tj
T*
(functioning as noun], Infinitives [to + verb], Participles\).) Tj
T*
(- Transitive verbs require a direct object \(e.g., 'The scientist synthesized the) Tj
T*
(peptide'\); Intransitive verbs do not take direct objects \(e.g., 'The precipitate) Tj
T*
(settled'\).) Tj
T*
(* Adjectives and Degree of Comparison: Positive, Comparative \(-er / more\), and) Tj
T*
(Superlative \(-est / most\). Avoid redundant double comparatives \(*more higher\).) Tj
T*
(* Adverbs: Modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverbs. Categorized by Manner) Tj
T*
(\(rapidly\), Frequency \(regularly\), Degree \(substantially\), and Time \(subsequently\).) Tj
T*
(* Prepositions: Spatial \(in, on, at, under, across\), Temporal \(at [exact time], on) Tj
T*
([days/dates], in [months/years/durations]\), and Directional \(into, onto, toward\).) Tj
T*
(- Between vs. Among: 'Between' is used for distinct individual entities \(typically) Tj
T*
(two\); 'Among' is used for collective groups of three or more.) Tj
T*
(* Conjunctions: Coordinating \(FANBOYS: For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So\),) Tj
T*
(Subordinating \(although, because, since, whereas, while\), Correlative \(either...or,) Tj
T*
(neither...nor, not only...but also\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 1: Error Identification and Correction in Technical Literature]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Identify and correct grammatical errors in the following four academic) Tj
T*
(biotechnology sentences, providing rigorous linguistic justifications.) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The laboratory purchased several new equipments and hardwares for the) Tj
T*
(molecular biology department.") Tj
T*
(- Error: 'equipments' and 'hardwares' are mass/uncountable nouns in standard) Tj
T*
(English; they do not possess plural -s forms.) Tj
T*
(- Correction: "The laboratory purchased several new pieces of equipment and) Tj
T*
(hardware for the molecular biology department.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The concentration of the solute in the beaker is more higher than the) Tj
T*
(surrounding matrix.") Tj
T*
