(- Error: 'more higher' is a redundant double comparative. The comparative form of) Tj
T*
(high is 'higher'.) Tj
T*
(- Correction: "The concentration of the solute in the beaker is significantly) Tj
T*
(higher than that of the surrounding matrix.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 3: "Each of the researchers have submitted their respective progress reports to) Tj
T*
(the principal investigator.") Tj
T*
(- Error: 'Each' is an indefinite pronoun that is grammatically singular and takes) Tj
T*
(a singular verb \('has'\).) Tj
T*
(- Correction: "Each of the researchers has submitted his or her progress report to) Tj
T*
(the principal investigator.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 4: "The enzyme solution was divided equally between the four test tubes.") Tj
T*
(- Error: 'Between' applies strictly to two distinct items; for four test tubes,) Tj
T*
('among' is required.) Tj
T*
(- Correction: "The enzyme solution was divided equally among the four test tubes.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 2: Prepositional Accuracy in Experimental Protocols]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Fill in the correct prepositions \(at, on, in, into, between, among, of, with\)) Tj
T*
(in the following scientific laboratory protocol:) Tj
T*
(Protocol Passage:) Tj
T*
("The experiment commenced [1] Monday morning [2] 09:00 AM. 5 mL of cell suspension was) Tj
T*
(transferred [3] a sterile centrifugation tube. The mixture was incubated [4] a constant) Tj
T*
(temperature [5] 37 deg C [6] a water bath for 48 hours. Variations in biomass yield were) Tj
T*
(observed [7] the three replicates.") Tj
T*
(Solution and Grammatical Rule:) Tj
T*
([1] on: 'on' is mandatory before days of the week \(on Monday\).) Tj
T*
([2] at: 'at' indicates specific points in time \(at 09:00 AM\).) Tj
T*
([3] into: 'into' indicates movement toward the interior of a container \(transferred) Tj
T*
(into\).) Tj
T*
([4] at: 'at' is used for specific physical measurements/temperatures \(at a constant) Tj
T*
(temperature\).) Tj
T*
([5] of: 'of' expresses quantity or specification \(of 37 deg C\).) Tj
T*
([6] in: 'in' denotes enclosure within an apparatus \(in a water bath\).) Tj
T*
([7] among: 'among' is required when distributing across three or more items \(among the) Tj
T*
(three replicates\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([EXERCISE 3: Correlative Conjunction Parallelism in Technical Writing]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Re-write the following sentences to enforce strict syntactic parallelism across) Tj
T*
(correlative conjunction pairs \(not only...but also, either...or, neither...nor\).) Tj
T*
(Sentence 1: "The newly designed bioreactor not only improved oxygen transfer rate, but) Tj
T*
(it also was reducing operational energy costs.") Tj
T*
(- Error: Asymmetric verb tenses. 'improved' \(simple past\) vs. 'was reducing' \(past) Tj
T*
(continuous\).) Tj
T*
(- Parallel Revision: "The newly designed bioreactor not only improved oxygen) Tj
T*
(transfer rate, but also reduced operational energy costs.") Tj
T*
(Sentence 2: "The technician must either recalibrate the spectrophotometer or the results) Tj
T*
(will be invalid.") Tj
T*
