([EXERCISE 4: Relative Pronoun Disambiguation: Restrictive vs. Non-Restrictive]) Tj
T*
(Problem: Contrast the meaning and punctuation of the relative clauses in the following) Tj
T*
(pair of sentences:) Tj
T*
(Sentence A: "The centrifuges that were manufactured in Germany operated without) Tj
T*
(vibration.") Tj
T*
(Sentence B: "The centrifuges, which were manufactured in Germany, operated without) Tj
T*
(vibration.") Tj
T*
(Analysis:) Tj
T*
(- Sentence A uses 'that' without commas \(Restrictive Clause\). The clause defines) Tj
T*
(WHICH specific centrifuges operated without vibration. Implication: The laboratory) Tj
T*
(owns multiple centrifuges; ONLY the subset manufactured in Germany operated) Tj
T*
(smoothly, whereas centrifuges from other countries did not.) Tj
T*
(- Sentence B uses 'which' enclosed in commas \(Non-Restrictive / Parenthetical) Tj
T*
(Clause\). The geographic origin is incidental background information. Implication:) Tj
T*
(ALL the laboratory's centrifuges operated without vibration; additionally, as a) Tj
T*
(matter of fact, they happen to have been manufactured in Germany.) Tj
T*
