(>> 1.2 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Define Countable and Uncountable nouns and list five common uncountable nouns) Tj
T*
(in scientific writing that are frequently misused with plural suffixes.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Countable nouns refer to discrete, individual entities that can be counted with) Tj
T*
(cardinal numbers, take indefinite articles \(a/an\) in the singular, and form regular or) Tj
T*
(irregular plurals \(e.g., pipette/pipettes, organism/organisms\). Uncountable \(mass\) nouns) Tj
T*
(refer to undifferentiated materials, concepts, or collective substances that cannot be) Tj
T*
(divided into separate units; they take singular verbs and cannot take indefinite) Tj
T*
(articles or plural suffixes. Five frequently misused uncountable nouns in technical) Tj
T*
(prose: \(1\) Equipment \(*equipments is incorrect; use 'pieces of equipment'\), \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Information \(*informations is incorrect; use 'pieces of data/information'\), \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Apparatus \(*apparatuses is incorrect when used as a mass noun\), \(4\) Research) Tj
T*
(\(*researches as a noun is incorrect; use 'research studies'\), \(5\) Software \(*softwares) Tj
T*
(is incorrect; use 'software programs'\).) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the syntactic rule of parallelism in technical English with) Tj
T*
(illustrative examples involving coordinating and correlative conjunctions.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Parallelism requires that two or more elements joined by coordinating) Tj
T*
(conjunctions \(and, but, or\) or correlative conjunctions \(either...or, neither...nor, not) Tj
T*
